    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-26--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-26: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.27";
    dc:description "P versus NP is a precise statement, so the obstacle is not vagueness. Nothing now public decides it: exhaustive solution of finite instances never yields a general polynomial bound or a general impossibility. The claim waits on a proof that does not exist, and computation and observation do not produce that proof.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The claim is that no polynomial-time procedure decides, for every instance, whether any path of a non-deterministic or multiway system yields a given outcome. A proof or a general polynomial algorithm would settle it; solving particular instances cannot.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A growing catalog of NP-complete problems is compatible with either answer.", "No finite computation decides whether every language in NP has a polynomial-time algorithm.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.78"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.265"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-26--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of wolfram2002-ch12-26 by Grok 4.7: 0.05";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
